<h3 id="call-for-papers"><strong>Call for Papers</strong></h3>

<p>With the rapid evolution of network security technologies, stealthy communication tunnels based on encryption protocols and low-rate covert attacks have become increasingly prevalent. Malicious traffic leveraging protocols like TLS poses serious challenges to traditional detection systems. To promote a cleaner and more secure cyberspace, we invite original research contributions that address detection and analysis of encrypted and covert network attacks.</p>

<p>This symposium will focus on the latest research theories and application methods of cyber pollution management, and collect the latest research results achieved by scholars, researchers, and frontline experts in related fields in the above mentioned areas. Potential topics include but are not limited to the following:</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    <p>Detection of TLS/SSL-based covert channels</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Identification of low-rate and stealthy network attacks</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Traffic analysis of encrypted malicious communications</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Machine learning and AI for encrypted traffic detection</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Real-time monitoring and classification of encrypted threats</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>Novel datasets and benchmarking methods</p>
  </li>
</ul>

